WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.757
Every request input should be treated as
untrusted until validated on the server.

2
00:00:08.837 --> 00:00:15.778
Path parameters, query parameters,
headers, cookies, JSON bodies,

3
00:00:15.858 --> 00:00:22.560
form submissions, and uploaded files can
all influence behavior.

4
00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:28.504
Frontend validation helps users correct
mistakes early,

5
00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:32.413
but it is not an enforcement boundary.

6
00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:38.477
Browser clients can be modified, requests
can be replayed,

7
00:00:38.557 --> 00:00:44.899
and API handlers can be called without the
intended interface.

8
00:00:44.979 --> 00:00:50.604
The server must validate before sensitive
processing.

9
00:00:50.684 --> 00:00:57.386
Schema validation concepts help make
request contracts visible.

10
00:00:57.466 --> 00:01:05.484
Handlers should check type, shape,
required fields, optional fields, length,

11
00:01:05.564 --> 00:01:12.146
range, format, enum values, and content
type where appropriate.

12
00:01:12.226 --> 00:01:18.448
Business-rule validation is separate from
type validation.

13
00:01:18.528 --> 00:01:26.307
A string may be a valid identifier format
but still refer to a resource the user

14
00:01:26.387 --> 00:01:27.943
cannot access.

15
00:01:28.023 --> 00:01:32.929
A number may be in range but still violate
policy.

16
00:01:33.009 --> 00:01:40.788
A form may be structurally valid but still
request an unauthorized mutation.

17
00:01:40.868 --> 00:01:48.527
API routes, route handlers, and server
actions should be explicit, narrow,

18
00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:50.282
and reviewable.

19
00:01:50.362 --> 00:01:56.825
Mutation paths need particular care
because they change state.

20
00:01:56.905 --> 00:02:04.444
The code should define which fields may be
updated, avoid mass assignment,

21
00:02:04.524 --> 00:02:07.276
apply request size limits,

22
00:02:07.356 --> 00:02:12.861
validate file uploads before downstream
processing,

23
00:02:12.941 --> 00:02:20.122
handle parsing errors safely, and return
consistent error responses.

24
00:02:20.202 --> 00:02:28.459
The handler should not rely on hidden
assumptions from the page that submitted the

25
00:02:28.539 --> 00:02:29.496
request.

26
00:02:29.576 --> 00:02:34.363
Safe validation is also an operations
feature.

27
00:02:34.443 --> 00:02:41.863
Clear request contracts make tests easier,
reduce surprising behavior,

28
00:02:41.943 --> 00:02:45.174
and give logs better structure.

29
00:02:45.254 --> 00:02:53.272
When validation fails, the response should
help the caller correct the request

30
00:02:53.352 --> 00:02:56.463
without revealing internals.

31
00:02:56.543 --> 00:03:01.570
Internal logs can record safe diagnostic
detail,

32
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:09.189
but they should avoid secrets, tokens,
session values, private payloads,

33
00:03:09.269 --> 00:03:12.500
and unnecessary personal data.
